IMPORT prelude

-- Insurance Act 1966 (Singapore) -- naming who gets my policy moneys: whether my policy is a "relevant policy" (s 131); a trust
-- nomination, what it shields from my creditors and whose consent I need to undo it (s 132); a revocable nomination, when it is
-- deemed revoked, how a nominee's death before me reshapes the shares, and where my death benefits go (s 133); and whom my insurer
-- may pay without probate when I die, and how a capped sum is shared among claimants (s 150(2), (7)-(13)).
--
-- SEAT: the policy owner -- the individual who owns a life policy or an accident and health policy on his or her own life and
-- decides who should benefit from it.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 9 March 2025, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/IA1966.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Authority's prescribed manner and requirements (asked as yes/no facts); trustee appointment (s 132(12)-(15));
-- variation of terms under a trust nomination (s 132(9)-(11)) beyond what s 132(7) shows; the insurer's register (s 134);
-- co-operative society policies (s 135); living benefits (s 150(1)); estate duty (s 150(3)-(6)); s 57 of the Probate and
-- Administration Act 1934, to which s 133(8)-(9) are subject. The amount prescribed for s 150(2)(b) is not deposited and is an input.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual to
-- whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test
-- pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Insurance Act 1966, Part 3C -- nomination of beneficiaries`

§§ `131 -- relevant policy`

-- s 131: "relevant policy" means any life policy or accident and health policy which (a) "is issued by a licensed insurer"; (b) "is
-- governed by Singapore law"; (c) "provides death benefits"; (d) "insures the life of the policy owner"; (e) is not the subject of
-- a trust under s 73 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886; and (f) is not an annuity bought with the CPF retirement sum
-- under s 15(6C) of the Central Provident Fund Act 1953.
-- s 132(1): the trust nomination does not apply to a relevant policy (a) issued under the Dependants' Protection Insurance Scheme;
-- (b) a CPF investment whose proceeds the member must repay into the CPF; or (c) prescribed by the Authority.

DECLARE `My policy` HAS
    `a life policy or an accident and health policy`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `issued by a licensed insurer`                                         IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `governed by Singapore law`                                            IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `provides death benefits`                                              IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `insures my own life`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
    `held on a trust under s 73 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act` IS A BOOLEAN -- (e)
    `an annuity bought with my CPF retirement sum`                         IS A BOOLEAN   -- (f)
    `issued under the Dependants' Protection Insurance Scheme`             IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 132(1)(a)
    `a CPF investment I must repay into the CPF`                           IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 132(1)(b)
    `of a kind the Authority has prescribed out of s 132`                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 132(1)(c)

GIVEN `my policy` IS A `My policy`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my policy a relevant policy` IF
        `my policy`'s `a life policy or an accident and health policy`
    AND `my policy`'s `issued by a licensed insurer`
    AND `my policy`'s `governed by Singapore law`
    AND `my policy`'s `provides death benefits`
    AND `my policy`'s `insures my own life`
    AND NOT `my policy`'s `held on a trust under s 73 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act`
    AND NOT `my policy`'s `an annuity bought with my CPF retirement sum`

GIVEN `my policy` IS A `My policy`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my policy carry a trust nomination` IF
        `Is my policy a relevant policy` `my policy`
    AND NOT `my policy`'s `issued under the Dependants' Protection Insurance Scheme`
    AND NOT `my policy`'s `a CPF investment I must repay into the CPF`
    AND NOT `my policy`'s `of a kind the Authority has prescribed out of s 132`

§§ `132, 133(2)-(3) -- making a nomination`

-- s 132(2): where the owner "who has attained the age of 18 years" (a) nominates "his or her spouse, his or her children, his or
-- her spouse and children or any of them"; (b) "expresses in the nomination his or her intention to create a trust"; and (c) makes
-- it, and indicates each nominee's portion, in the prescribed manner -- "the nomination creates a trust of the policy moneys".
-- (3): "No nomination under subsection (2) is valid unless it provides for the disposition of all policy moneys".
-- s 133(1): s 133 does not apply to a policy carrying a s 132 nomination not revoked under s 132(7).
-- s 133(2): an owner aged 18 or more "may nominate any person" for the whole or any portion of the death benefits, in the
-- prescribed manner; (3): not valid unless it disposes of "all death benefits".
-- Portions are given as percentages; "all" is read as portions adding to 100.

DECLARE Nominee HAS
    `who`                             IS A STRING
    `my spouse`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `my child`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `portion in percent`              IS A NUMBER
    `died before me`                  IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Nomination kind` IS ONE OF
    `a trust nomination`              -- s 132: irrevocable without consents; creates a trust
    `a revocable nomination`          -- s 133: I can change it at any time

DECLARE `My nomination` HAS
    `kind`                                                            IS A `Nomination kind`
    `nominees`                                                        IS A LIST OF Nominee
    `my age when I nominated`                                         IS A NUMBER
    `I expressed an intention to create a trust of the policy moneys` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made in the prescribed manner, giving each nominee's portion`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `an earlier trust nomination of mine on this policy still stands` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the nominees` IS A LIST OF Nominee
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total of the portions of` MEANS sum (map (GIVEN n YIELD n's `portion in percent`) `the nominees`)

GIVEN `the nominee` IS A Nominee
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is my spouse or child` MEANS `the nominee`'s `my spouse` OR `the nominee`'s `my child`

GIVEN `my policy` IS A `My policy`, `my nomination` IS A `My nomination`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my nomination valid` IF
        `my nomination`'s `my age when I nominated` AT LEAST 18
    AND `my nomination`'s `made in the prescribed manner, giving each nominee's portion`
    AND `the total of the portions of` (`my nomination`'s `nominees`) EQUALS 100
    AND CONSIDER `my nomination`'s `kind`
        WHEN `a trust nomination` THEN
                `Can my policy carry a trust nomination` `my policy`
            AND all `is my spouse or child` (`my nomination`'s `nominees`)
            AND `my nomination`'s `I expressed an intention to create a trust of the policy moneys`
        WHEN `a revocable nomination` THEN
                `Is my policy a relevant policy` `my policy`
            AND NOT `my nomination`'s `an earlier trust nomination of mine on this policy still stands`

§§ `132(4)-(5) -- what a trust nomination keeps from my creditors`

-- s 132(4): policy moneys subject to the trust "do not form part of the estate of the policy owner and are not subject to his or her
-- debts". (5): "If it is proved that the relevant policy was effected, and the premiums ... were paid, with intent to defraud the
-- creditors of the policy owner, the creditors are entitled to receive out of the policy moneys a sum equal to the premiums so paid."
-- Whether fraud is proved is for a court: an input. Where there is no valid trust nomination s 132(4) does not shield anything and the
-- general law of my estate decides; this encoding returns NOTHING for that case rather than guess.

GIVEN `my policy`                                                         IS A `My policy`
      `my nomination`                                                     IS A `My nomination`
      `a court finds the policy was taken and paid for to defraud my creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the premiums I paid`                                               IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What can my creditors take from my trust policy moneys` IS
    IF `my nomination is a valid trust nomination`
    THEN IF   `a court finds the policy was taken and paid for to defraud my creditors`
         THEN JUST `the premiums I paid`
         ELSE JUST 0
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `my nomination is a valid trust nomination` MEANS
                `Is my nomination valid` `my policy` `my nomination`
            AND CONSIDER `my nomination`'s `kind`
                WHEN `a trust nomination` THEN TRUE
                OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `132(7) -- undoing a trust nomination`

-- s 132(7): the owner "may revoke a nomination under subsection (2) if, and only if, the prior written consent to the revocation has
-- been obtained from" (a) where any trustee of the policy moneys is a person other than the owner, (i) that trustee (or any one of
-- them), or (ii) "so long as no nominee has died before the revocation", each nominee aged 18 or more and a parent or guardian
-- ("not being the policy owner") of each nominee under 18; (b) in any other case, "so long as no nominee has died before the
-- revocation", the same nominees and parents or guardians; and (c) the prescribed requirements are met.
-- (10): a revocation in contravention of (7) "is void".
-- Once a nominee has died and no outside trustee exists, (b) names no one: only (c) remains.

DECLARE `Consent I need to revoke` IS ONE OF
    `an outside trustee, or else every adult nominee and a parent or guardian of every minor nominee`
    `an outside trustee`
    `every adult nominee and a parent or guardian of every minor nominee`
    `no one is named, only the prescribed requirements`

GIVEN `a trustee of the policy moneys is someone other than me` IS A BOOLEAN, `a nominee has died` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Consent I need to revoke`
DECIDE `Whose written consent do I need to revoke my trust nomination` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `a trustee of the policy moneys is someone other than me` AND NOT `a nominee has died`
            THEN `an outside trustee, or else every adult nominee and a parent or guardian of every minor nominee`
        IF `a trustee of the policy moneys is someone other than me`
            THEN `an outside trustee`
        IF NOT `a nominee has died`
            THEN `every adult nominee and a parent or guardian of every minor nominee`
        OTHERWISE `no one is named, only the prescribed requirements`

GIVEN `a trustee of the policy moneys is someone other than me`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `a nominee has died`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `an outside trustee consented in writing beforehand`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `every adult nominee and a parent or guardian of each minor consented in writing beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed requirements for revocation are met`                   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I revoke my trust nomination` IF
        `the prescribed requirements for revocation are met`
    AND CONSIDER `Whose written consent do I need to revoke my trust nomination` `a trustee of the policy moneys is someone other than me` `a nominee has died`
        WHEN `an outside trustee, or else every adult nominee and a parent or guardian of every minor nominee`
            THEN `an outside trustee consented in writing beforehand`
                 OR `every adult nominee and a parent or guardian of each minor consented in writing beforehand`
        WHEN `an outside trustee`
            THEN `an outside trustee consented in writing beforehand`
        WHEN `every adult nominee and a parent or guardian of every minor nominee`
            THEN `every adult nominee and a parent or guardian of each minor consented in writing beforehand`
        WHEN `no one is named, only the prescribed requirements`
            THEN TRUE

§§ `133(5)-(7) -- when a revocable nomination changes or falls away`

-- s 133(7): a s 133 nomination "is deemed to be revoked if" (a) the owner "assigns, encumbers or otherwise deals with" the policy or
-- an interest under it; (b) after the nomination, the owner makes a will under the Wills Act 1838 which (i) disposes of "all death
-- benefits" and (ii) specifies the prescribed particulars of the policy; or (c) after it, the owner makes another s 133 nomination or a
-- s 132 nomination.
-- s 133(5)(a): if a nominee dies before the owner and "there is no surviving nominee, the nomination is deemed to be revoked".

GIVEN `I have assigned, encumbered or otherwise dealt with the policy`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `I later made a will disposing of all the death benefits and giving the prescribed particulars`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `I later made another nomination on the policy`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
      `every nominee died before me`                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my revocable nomination deemed revoked` IF
        `I have assigned, encumbered or otherwise dealt with the policy`
    OR  `I later made a will disposing of all the death benefits and giving the prescribed particulars`
    OR  `I later made another nomination on the policy`
    OR  `every nominee died before me`

-- s 133(5)(b)-(c): where a nominee dies before the owner, each surviving nominee's portion is increased by a share of the deceased
-- nominee's portion, "A / B x C", where A is "that surviving nominee's original portion", B "the aggregate of all the surviving
-- nominees' original portions" and C "the deceased nominee's portion". (The text layer prints the fraction as A over B; read from its
-- layout.) With one survivor A = B, so the survivor takes the whole of C, as (b) says. Several deceased nominees are taken one C at a
-- time; with the same B each time the shares simply add.

GIVEN `the nominees` IS A LIST OF Nominee
GIVETH A LIST OF Nominee
`the surviving nominees among` MEANS filter (GIVEN n YIELD NOT n's `died before me`) `the nominees`

GIVEN `the nominees` IS A LIST OF Nominee
GIVETH A LIST OF Nominee
`the deceased nominees among` MEANS filter (GIVEN n YIELD n's `died before me`) `the nominees`

GIVEN `the nominees` IS A LIST OF Nominee
      `the name`     IS A STRING
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What share of my death benefits does this nominee now take` IS
    IF `B` EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE `A` PLUS (`A` DIVIDED BY `B`) TIMES `C`
    WHERE
        `A` MEANS `the total of the portions of` (filter (GIVEN n YIELD n's `who` EQUALS `the name`) (`the surviving nominees among` `the nominees`))
        `B` MEANS `the total of the portions of` (`the surviving nominees among` `the nominees`)
        `C` MEANS `the total of the portions of` (`the deceased nominees among` `the nominees`)

-- s 133(6): where the owner and nominees die "in circumstances rendering it uncertain which of them survived the other", then "in the
-- absence of any order of the court determining otherwise" the deaths are presumed to occur "in order of seniority" and "the younger is
-- deemed to have survived the elder". A court order is the court's call: NOTHING, not a guess.

GIVEN `the nominee in fact died before me`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order of our deaths is uncertain`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nominee was older than me`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court has ordered otherwise`                   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the nominee treated as having died before me` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the order of our deaths is uncertain`    THEN JUST `the nominee in fact died before me`
        IF `a court has ordered otherwise`               THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE                                             JUST `the nominee was older than me`

§§ `133(8)-(9) -- where my death benefits go`

-- s 133(8): "Despite anything in the Wills Act 1838, the Intestate Succession Act 1967 and any rule of law", where the owner made
-- s 133 nominations and wills: (a) if the last nomination is not and is not deemed revoked, by the last nomination; (b) if it is, and
-- the last will is not revoked, by the last will; (c) if both are revoked, by the Intestate Succession Act 1967. (9): the same where the
-- owner dies intestate, without (b).
-- A valid, unrevoked trust nomination takes the policy moneys out of my estate into the trust (s 132(2), (4)); s 133 does not apply
-- (s 133(1)). With no s 133 nomination at all, s 133(8)-(9) say nothing and the general law (not deposited) decides.

DECLARE `Where my death benefits go` IS ONE OF
    `to my nominees, on the trust my nomination created`
    `as my last nomination says`
    `as my last will says`
    `under the Intestate Succession Act 1967`
    `not decided by s 133`

GIVEN `my trust nomination stands`                             IS A BOOLEAN
      `I made a revocable nomination`                          IS A BOOLEAN
      `my last revocable nomination is or is deemed revoked`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `I made a will`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
      `my last will is revoked`                                IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Where my death benefits go`
DECIDE `Where will my death benefits go` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `my trust nomination stands`                                        THEN `to my nominees, on the trust my nomination created`
        IF NOT `I made a revocable nomination`                                 THEN `not decided by s 133`
        IF NOT `my last revocable nomination is or is deemed revoked`          THEN `as my last nomination says`
        IF `I made a will` AND NOT `my last will is revoked`                   THEN `as my last will says`
        OTHERWISE                                                                   `under the Intestate Succession Act 1967`

§ `Insurance Act 1966, s 150 -- payment without probate when I die`

-- s 150(2): when the owner dies and death benefits are payable, (a) if (7), (8) or (9) applies the insurer "may make one or more payments
-- ... without the production of any probate or letters of administration"; (b) if (10) applies, it may pay under (10) and (11), the
-- payments "not exceeding in the aggregate the amount prescribed by the Authority"; (c) the insurer is discharged.
-- (7): an unrevoked s 132 nomination of which the insurer has written notice -- pay (d) an outside trustee for every nominee, or (e) an
-- adult nominee, a parent or guardian (not the owner) of a minor nominee, or a dead nominee's personal representatives, up to "that
-- nominee's portion".
-- (8): a s 133 nomination "not and ... not deemed to be revoked", notified -- the same nominees, up to their portions.
-- (9): "Subject to subsection (7)", an unrevoked will disposing of all death benefits with the prescribed particulars, notified by a
-- notice "signed by the policy owner" -- pay "any executor of that will", up to the whole death benefits.
-- (10): where (a) the owner "has not made" any nomination or any such will; (b) the insurer "has not received" notice of any
-- nomination or of any such will; or (c) prescribed circumstances exist -- pay "any proper claimant".
-- READINGS: "has not made (i) ... or (ii) ..." and "has not received (i) ... or (ii) ..." are read as "neither". (9) is said to be
-- subject to (7) only; this encoding puts (8) before (9) too, since an unrevoked s 133 nomination governs under s 133(8)(a). Both are
-- inferences.

DECLARE `What my insurer knows when I die` HAS
    `a trust nomination of mine stands unrevoked`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `a revocable nomination of mine stands, not deemed revoked`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insurer has written notice of that nomination`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `a trustee of the policy moneys is someone other than me`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `I made a nomination at all`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `I made a will disposing of all death benefits with the prescribed particulars`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `that will is unrevoked`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insurer has written notice of that will signed by me`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insurer has written notice of any nomination or such will`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `circumstances the Authority has prescribed exist`                                IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Who may be paid without probate` IS ONE OF
    `the outside trustee, for every nominee`
    `each nominee or a minor nominee's parent or guardian or a dead nominee's personal representatives, up to that nominee's portion`
    `an executor of my will, up to the whole death benefits`
    `any proper claimant, within the prescribed aggregate`
    `no one: probate or letters of administration are needed`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `What my insurer knows when I die`
GIVETH A `Who may be paid without probate`
DECIDE `Whom may my insurer pay without probate when I die` IS
    BRANCH
        IF      `the facts`'s `a trust nomination of mine stands unrevoked`
            AND `the facts`'s `the insurer has written notice of that nomination`
            THEN IF   `the facts`'s `a trustee of the policy moneys is someone other than me`
                 THEN `the outside trustee, for every nominee`
                 ELSE `each nominee or a minor nominee's parent or guardian or a dead nominee's personal representatives, up to that nominee's portion`
        IF      `the facts`'s `a revocable nomination of mine stands, not deemed revoked`
            AND `the facts`'s `the insurer has written notice of that nomination`
            THEN `each nominee or a minor nominee's parent or guardian or a dead nominee's personal representatives, up to that nominee's portion`
        IF      `the facts`'s `I made a will disposing of all death benefits with the prescribed particulars`
            AND `the facts`'s `that will is unrevoked`
            AND `the facts`'s `the insurer has written notice of that will signed by me`
            THEN `an executor of my will, up to the whole death benefits`
        IF      (NOT `the facts`'s `I made a nomination at all` AND NOT `the facts`'s `I made a will disposing of all death benefits with the prescribed particulars`)
            OR  NOT `the facts`'s `the insurer has written notice of any nomination or such will`
            OR  `the facts`'s `circumstances the Authority has prescribed exist`
            THEN `any proper claimant, within the prescribed aggregate`
        OTHERWISE `no one: probate or letters of administration are needed`

§§ `150(12)-(13) -- proper claimant`

-- s 150(12): "proper claimant" means a person who (a) claims "as executor of the deceased"; or (b) claims and "is the widower, widow,
-- parent, child, brother, sister, nephew or niece of the deceased". (13): "an illegitimate person is treated as the legitimate child of
-- his or her actual parents".

DECLARE `The claimant is` IS ONE OF
    `the executor of my will`
    `my widow or widower`
    `my parent`
    `my child`
    `my child born outside marriage`
    `my brother or sister`
    `my nephew or niece`
    `my grandchild`
    `my cousin`
    `my aunt or uncle`
    `a friend`

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A `The claimant is`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this claimant a proper claimant` IF
    CONSIDER `the claimant`
    WHEN `my grandchild`      THEN FALSE
    WHEN `my cousin`          THEN FALSE
    WHEN `my aunt or uncle`   THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a friend`           THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `150(11) -- sharing the prescribed amount among several claims`

-- s 150(11): where (10) applies and the insurer "receives 2 or more different claims", (a) each is paid "in the same order of priority";
-- (b) the amount for each is "A / B x C", A being the claim paid in full, B the total of all claims paid in full, and C "the amount
-- prescribed by the Authority". The prescribed amount is not deposited: an input.
-- The formula is applied as written. Read literally, it shares out the whole of C even where the claims total less than C, so a claim
-- can be paid more than its full amount; the text sets no "lesser of". With one claim, (11) does not apply and (2)(b) caps the payment
-- at the prescribed aggregate.

GIVEN `the number of claims`                      IS A NUMBER
      `this claim in full`                        IS A NUMBER
      `all the claims in full`                    IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed amount`                     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much may a proper claimant be paid without probate` IS
    IF `the number of claims` AT LEAST 2
    THEN (`this claim in full` DIVIDED BY `all the claims in full`) TIMES `the prescribed amount`
    ELSE IF `this claim in full` AT MOST `the prescribed amount`
         THEN `this claim in full`
         ELSE `the prescribed amount`
